                        7169 --2293:  *    #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0DPC, #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0DPS, #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0DPW (Used by sub functions)
                        7170 --2294:  * \par Precondition
                        7171 --2295:  *  - #PKCD_EDDSA_PDT_P, #PKCD_EDDSA_R2MODP, #PKCD_EDDSA_PWORK must have been prepared.
                        7172 --2296:  *  - #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0OMR (DL bit), #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0DPW value must have been set beforehand.
                        7173 --2297:  * \par Detailed description
                        7174 --2298:  *      - Operates scalar multiplication of the projective coordinate base point on Twisted Edwards Curve.
                        7175 --2299:  *      - The scalar multiplication is done using the binary method.
                        7176 --2300:  * \par Remarks
                        7177 --2301:  *  - None
                        7178 --2302:  *
                        7179 --2303:  * Pseudo-code for the function can be found below. Some values are represented in Montgomery format.
                        7180 --2304:  * -# Initialize the variable ret with #PKCD_RET_INTERNALERR.
                        7181 --2305:  * -# If #PKCD_CFG_USE_ED25519_PRECALC_TABLE_16 is declared, the loop of the window method is done
                        7182 --2306:  *      {curve25519 bit size}/4 times .
                        7183 --2307:  *    And if #PKCD_CFG_USE_ED25519_PRECALC_TABLE_256 is declared, the loop of the window method is done
                        7184 --2308:  *      {curve25519 bit size}/16 times.
                        7185 --2309:  * -# If p_executed_bits == 0 Then prepare neutral element (0, 1, 1) for temporary value as follows,
                        7186 --2310:  *   -# Set #PKCD_EDDSA_PDT_P as PKCC DPT area.
                        7187 --2311:  *   -# Clear an x-coordinate value with #r_pkcd_cmn_ram_clr.
                        7188 --2312:  *   -# Calculate R for a y-coordinate with #r_pkcd_cmn_ARInvModC.
                        7189 --2313:  *   -# Copy R for a z-coordinate with #r_pkcd_cmn_cpy_by_64bounds.
                        7190 --2314:  * -# Set the neutral element as the adding point for the case of a target bit in binary method == 0.
                        7191 --2315:  * -# Set the P1 as the adding point for the case of a target bit in binary method == 1.
                        7192 --2316:  * -# Use the number at p_executed_bits as the starting index of the bit for the binary method.
                        7193 --2317:  * -# Derive the last index of the bit for the binary method from processing bits.
                        7194 --2318:  * -# For the bits between the starting index and the last index of the given scalar, do following
                        7195 --2319:  *   -# Assume the scalar value separated into 4 or 16 parts, and acquire the each bit at the loop index
                        7196 --2320:  *      of the separated parts.
                        7197 --2321:  *      For example if scalar value is separated into 4 parts, bit[192+idx], bit[128+idx], bit[64+idx] and
                        7198 --2322:  *      bit[0+idx] are acquired.
                        7199 --2323:  *      And in this case, 2^(192+idx)+2^(128+idx)+2^(64+idx)+2^(0+idx) is used for the window value.
                        7200 --2324:  *      All the scalar multiplication result with base point and available window values
                        7201 --2325:  *      are prepared as g_ed25519_comb_table_16 and g_ed25519_comb_table_256.
                        7202 --2326:  *   -# Double the point in the temporary area.
                        7203 --2327:  *   -# Add an {base point} x {window value} result to the point in the temporary area.
                        7204 --2328:  * -# Extract the return value from ret with #r_pkcd_cmn_extract_result, and set ret to it.
                        7205 --2329:  * -# If the value of the return code variable is #PKCD_RET_OK Then,
                        7206 --2330:  *   -# Update the number at p_executed_bits with resulting loop index.
                        7207 --2331:  *   -# If the updated number is not equal to curve field size,
                        7208 --2332:  *     -# Set #PKCD_RET_PROCESSING into the return code variable.
                        7209 --2333:  *   -# Else,
                        7210 --2334:  *     -# All the bits executed, so copy result into p_p3.
                        7211 --2335:  * -# Return ret
                        7212 --2336:  *
                        7213 --2337:  * \callgraph
                        7214 --2338:  *********************************************************************************************************************/
